
For pure water, Quintana & Haymet (Chem Phys Lett 189, 273 (1992))
compared Ewald and spherical cutoffs and found no difference for the
free energy of the SPC and CF models.

Kollman et al (JCP 101, 7953 (1994)) compared reaction field and
spherical cutoff and found little (5%) higher free energy for TIP3P
water with the reaction field. I think they have ca. 3% noise.

I have compared spherical cutoff at 8.5 A and reaction field for
TIP4P water. For 267 waters, I get 1-2% effects:
                Ave E     Ave Volume
No Rxn Field    -10.05       30.45 A^3
With Rxn Field   -9.84       30.02
 
Berendsen et al have also looked at several water models with 
spherical cutoff, reaction field and 9 and 12 A cutoffs. They
generally find less than 0.5% differences for energy and density
between the various combinations. Diffusion constants are ca.
0.2 x 10^-5 cm^2/s higher with the reaction field, e.g.,
3.7 vs 3.9 for TIP4P (JCP 108, 10220 (1998)).

